A test is marked as PASS when:
- The actual result matches the expected result
- The function behaves correctly
- No unexpected errors occur
A test is marked as FAIL when:
- The actual output differs from expected output
- System behavior is incorrect
- Required functionality is missing
A test is marked as ERROR when:
- The application crashes
- Runtime exceptions occur
- System cannot continue execution
